    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d154">

                <pb facs="0335" n="207" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg207"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 154</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Scruggs</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-02-25"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 25,
                        1885</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 22.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I herewith transmit a copy of a dispatch,
                    No. 122, of January 7 last from the United States consul at Barranquilla, in
                    relation to the revolution then in progress in Colombia, and have to say that
                    while the question of accountability for the spoliation of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">insurgents</hi> may remain open, yet there can be no
                    doubt as to the responsibility of the Government <hi rendition="#italic">de
                        jure</hi> for all spoliations it may resort to for its own protection.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d154-a1.xml" xpointer="d154-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
